{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RjbAwqPbeSS5DESKcEKMUn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the two member documents — `foreman.config.json` and the `EXECUTION-LOG.md` — plus the plan/description they anchor to:\n\n## runtime-host — build trio session summary (grounded claims)\n\n**What the session set out to build**\n- The target is the **missing Tier-1 deterministic runtime host** for the already-shipped Gandalf v1 skill — the \"thin runtime entry\" the prior build log flagged as an open follow-up (`DESCRIPTION.md:1-13`).\n- Its job: take a live Gandalf analysis's **RAW, un-stamped draft** and run it through the **already-shipped seam engine** (`seam/*.mjs`) to emit a **canary-conformant, honestly-graded** output validated by the shipped `assertIncrement1Conformant` (`DESCRIPTION.md:3-9`).\n- Stated motivation: make Gandalf's grades **deterministic rather than model-self-asserted** — the authors' first real run showed the model \"keeps hand-approximating tier stamps and failing the canary\" without this host (`DESCRIPTION.md:11-13`).\n\n**Foreman build configuration (`foreman.config.json`)**\n- Project `gandalf-runtime-host`; docs = DESCRIPTION / IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN / EXECUTION-LOG.\n- Gate command: `node --test test/*.test.mjs`; `cwd` set two levels up (`../..`, i.e. the gandalf skill root); **`git: false`** (Foreman runs without committing in this config).\n\n**Scope discipline locked at intake**\n- **Tier-1 only / deterministic.** The host runs the seam pass on **one** model run; it does **not** dispatch the live independent named-defeater refuters or the researchPrime SITUATE commission — those need the `agent()` seam the repo marks as \"the integration point the gate never runs\" (`DESCRIPTION.md:15-24`).\n- Honest grading floor: every **elevation** lands at **SPECULATIVE** with `NO_INDEPENDENT_REFUTATION_STAMP`; diagnosis findings keep their evidence rungs + `gandalf_core` provenance; `risk_labels` capped at single-family **PROMISING** (`cross_model:false`); only **REFUTED** drops (`DESCRIPTION.md:18-22`).\n- **Reuse, never fork** the shipped seams (refute / score-label / diagnose-core / anticipate / situate / harness); the host adds glue + a CLI entry and \"invents no new grading logic\" (`DESCRIPTION.md:26-32`).\n- Additive-only footprint: new `runtime/` dir, new `test/runtime-*.test.mjs`, doc touches to `SKILL.md §RUNTIME` / `LESSONS.md` / `journal/` (`DESCRIPTION.md:44-45`).\n\n**Planned wave structure (3 waves, terminal milestone = Wave 3)**\n- **Wave 1** — `runtime/seam-pass.mjs` exporting pure `applySeamPass(rawDraft, {cross_model=false})`; malformed draft throws named `SeamPassInputError` (no fabrication) (`IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md:8-37`).\n- **Wave 2** — `runtime/gandalf-run.mjs` CLI (`--input`/stdin → `--output`/stdout) + `RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md`; malformed input → non-zero exit, honest stderr, **no partial output** (`IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md:39-60`).\n- **Wave 3** — end-to-end integration test + docs flip (`SKILL.md §RUNTIME` from \"aspirational\" to a real pointer) (`IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md:62-72`).\n\n**Pre-build state recorded in the Execution Log**\n- Baseline to re-verify at build start: Gandalf v1 shipped, gate = **130/130** canary tests (`EXECUTION-LOG.md:9`).\n- Gate is deterministic; the live-refuter `agent()` dispatch is explicitly **out of scope and out of the gate** (`EXECUTION-LOG.md:8`).\n- HALT-worthy / reserved surfaces: any change to shipped seams/schema/canary, or reaching for the `agent()` live-refuter seam (that is the follow-on Tier-2) (`EXECUTION-LOG.md:10-11`).\n\n**Honest gap in the member documents**\n- The `EXECUTION-LOG.md` contains **only the Crucible-seeded pre-build block** — there are **no Foreman per-wave EXECUTE→GATE→REVIEW→FIX→verdict entries below the seed line** (`EXECUTION-LOG.md:3-14`). So these member docs capture the **framing/plan of the session, not a recorded completed-build trace.**\n- (Out of scope for the two member docs, but for context: the branch's git log — `cd24857 \"land the Tier-1 deterministic runtime host\"`, plus two follow-up hardening commits — indicates the host was in fact landed; that history just isn't reflected inside this Execution Log, consistent with `git:false` in the config.)\n\nWould you like me to verify the actual build outcome (run the gate / inspect `runtime/`), or keep this strictly to the planning-document summary?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8813,"cache_read_input_tokens":30745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8813},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fea3ae45-11f6-4dcb-b1f2-04df8c8061cd","uuid":"d3f5af11-1345-48db-842e-58907aaf4cae","request_id":"req_011CcLjoo1QvqacsfjgQ8i2J"}
